# Network and API

Purpose: HTTP access against `hms-backend` per [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc).

## Mandatory rules

- Repository contracts in domain layer; no HTTP from UI.
- Use `dio` for clients and interceptors.
- DTOs in data layer with `snake_case` JSON mapping.
- Map API errors to app failures before UI.
- Apply request timeouts; support cancellation for stale requests.
- No logging of tokens, passwords, or sensitive payloads.
- Handle `401` through session manager.
- Environment-driven base URLs and timeouts.
- HTTP owns CRUD mutations; WebSocket listeners refresh UI after server broadcasts (see [`realtime_sync.mdc`](./realtime_sync.mdc)).

## Client layout

```txt
core/network/
├── api_client.dart
├── api_endpoints.dart
├── api_interceptors.dart
├── api_result.dart
└── network_failure_mapper.dart
```

